  "_notes": "Wiimote pointer (ir_x/ir_y) is on the right stick by default: every pad has one, and the stick is free in Wiimote and Nunchuk modes. Gyro pointing is opt-in through the gyro-aim preset (options.gyro mode 'pointer'). The Wiimote is modelled held upright (A main, B trigger on r2). Sideways NES-style games want two=face_east, one=face_south; that is a per-game rule, not a separate controller type. tilt is accel-driven where the pad has an accelerometer, otherwise unbound. On the Classic Controller, L/R are the analog triggers, so they take l2/r2 and the digital ZL/ZR take l1/r1. That is the opposite of the Classic Controller Pro's physical layout; review. label_positions here describes the Classic Controller only: Wiimote a/b aren't on a compass. meta targets wiimote_nunchuk, the default, because most Wii games use it."
